{"root":"pli/ms","translators":["sujato"],"title":"Meṇḍasira","html":"<article id='thag1.78'><header><ul><li class='division'><span class='root'>Theragāthā 1.78 </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Verses of the Senior Monks 1.78 </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Ekakanipāta </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The Book of the Ones </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Aṭṭhamavagga </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Chapter Eight </span></li></ul>\n<h1 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Meṇḍasirattheragāthā </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Meṇḍasira </span></h1></header>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>“Anekajātisaṁsāraṁ, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Transmigrating through countless rebirths, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>sandhāvissaṁ anibbisaṁ; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>I’ve journeyed without reward. </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Tassa me dukkhajātassa, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>I’ve suffered, but now </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>dukkhakkhandho aparaddho”ti. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>the mass of suffering has fallen away. </span></span></p></blockquote>\n<p class='endsutta'><span class='root'>… Meṇḍasiro thero …. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></p></article>"}
